1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,336
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:08,425
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,635
- ♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:19,144
[Olga] <i>You're Ibyang's real father.</i>

7
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:20,270
<i>She's your child, Atoy.</i>

8
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:24,023
[Ibyang] <i>If Mama Olga isn't my mother…</i>

9
00:00:24,107 --> 00:00:24,983
PREVIOUSLY

10
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:26,151
<i>…then who?</i>

11
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:28,236
[Audrey] <i>You're my baby girl.</i>

12
00:00:28,319 --> 00:00:30,405
[Atoy] I never prayed
<i>for anything else but…</i>

13
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:31,865
to have my family whole again.

14
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:33,700
[Nestor] The child of thread!

15
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:35,368
- Long live!
- [all] Long live!

16
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:37,579
That means
he might already be with Audrey.

17
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:39,706
Good. I'll take them all down at once.

18
00:00:39,789 --> 00:00:41,916
[Ibyang] <i>I still can't believe it.</i>

19
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,920
I've been with my parents all along.

20
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:47,464
[Audrey] Us too, child.

21
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,257
[Gavin] <i>Do you like Karla?</i>

22
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:52,135
- Why, bro? You, do you like Karla?
- Yes.

23
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:53,720
[Uno]
<i>Then why did you choose someone else?</i>

24
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:55,889
Sorry also for being strict with you.

25
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:59,225
You'll be a best actress someday.

26
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:01,227
[Ibyang] You're so good at crying!

27
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:04,439
Of course,
I already consider you as my mother.

28
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,984
Let's just forget
everything that happened.

29
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:09,486
- [Cita] <i>Because there's a feast prepared--</i>
- [Atoy] Eh, I'm so hungry--

30
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:12,614
<i>…Father Peping and Captain prepared</i>
<i>a feast for you,</i>

31
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:14,741
<i>- to celebrate your return.</i>
- [phone rings]

32
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:15,742
[in English] Hello, sir?

33
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:19,370
[theme music concludes]

34
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:20,914
[Denden] Which do you prefer?

35
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:22,415
Sago or agar-agar?

36
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:25,752
I prefer sago, because you can chew it.

37
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:27,587
Me, I prefer agar-agar

38
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:30,381
because it's soft on the throat.

39
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:31,549
Smooth! [chuckles]

40
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,427
But, who's yummier?

41
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:36,137
Gavin or Uno?

42
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:39,182
But me, if you ask me…

43
00:01:39,265 --> 00:01:41,226
If I weren't a lesbian…

44
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:42,811
[both] Uno!

45
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:45,188
[pleasant music playing]

46
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:48,650
Of course, Emerson is first, next is Uno.

47
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:50,693
You, Karla? Do you also like Uno?

48
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:52,320
[music fades]

49
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:54,906
Hmm. Admit it, Karla!

50
00:01:54,989 --> 00:01:56,825
You also like Uno. [smirks]

51
00:01:56,908 --> 00:01:59,661
If it's just a crush, Uno is fine.

52
00:01:59,744 --> 00:02:01,496
But like?

53
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:02,956
I don't like Uno that way.

54
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:06,709
Hmm. So, Gavin is really your bet?

55
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:08,461
Sis, for a long time.

56
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:11,339
I even feel he likes me too.

57
00:02:12,048 --> 00:02:13,716
He seems jealous of Uno now.

58
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:17,679
Maybe he realized he likes me too.

59
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,764
- [grunts]
- [sneaky music playing]

60
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:21,516
You know, Karla, you're wrong.

61
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:23,101
If a guy really likes you,

62
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:25,228
you won't be confused
whether he likes you or not.

63
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:27,272
He'll tell you directly.

64
00:02:28,273 --> 00:02:30,275
- [in English] Correct.
- Mm.

65
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:33,027
But Gavin still seems taken.

66
00:02:33,111 --> 00:02:34,696
I saw him with Cathy,

67
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:35,989
they were together earlier.

68
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:37,073
[T-Bak smirks]

69
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:39,701
Gavin is really something else, huh?

70
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:42,662
He has a girlfriend,
but still flirts with someone else.

71
00:02:42,745 --> 00:02:43,955
He's a "playah"!

72
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:45,123
[chuckles]

73
00:02:45,623 --> 00:02:47,625
[T-Bak] Playah. Help me here.

74
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:49,961
[in English] Gavin!
Gavin, will you just stop?!

75
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:51,504
[sneaky music fades]

76
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:52,505
[in English] Look, Cathy!

77
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:55,508
I don't think our relationship
will work out anymore.

78
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:56,676
I think this is where it ends.

79
00:02:57,343 --> 00:02:58,219
[in English] What?!

80
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,221
So, you're dumping me?!

81
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:03,558
No one has ever done this to me!

82
00:03:03,641 --> 00:03:04,601
[in English] How dare you!

83
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:05,810
Why are you doing this?!

84
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:07,103
Is it because of Karla?!

85
00:03:07,186 --> 00:03:09,230
Cathy, can you please
listen to me first? Please!

86
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:10,231
[heavy music playing]

87
00:03:10,315 --> 00:03:12,817
I think it's not fair to you to enter
a relationship where the guy

88
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:13,985
is already half-hearted.

89
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:15,445
So, it is Karla then?

90
00:03:17,488 --> 00:03:20,366
You know what, you two just get together.

91
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:26,956
[heavy music fades]

92
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,416
[Mercado] Padua.

93
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:31,628
You almost didn't make it.

94
00:03:32,378 --> 00:03:33,880
We were all worried.

95
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:37,800
[in English] But I'm glad you're safe.

96
00:03:38,509 --> 00:03:42,680
And I heard…
you've reunited with your family.

97
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:43,598
Uno told me.

98
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:45,975
[sighs]

99
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:47,143
[in English] Yes, sir.

100
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,145
[smirks, in English] I'm happy for you.

101
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:50,396
Ah, sit down first.

102
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:51,856
[in English] Thank you.

103
00:03:55,693 --> 00:03:56,945
Uh…

104
00:03:57,946 --> 00:04:03,451
As much as I'd like to give you
a long time to be with them…

105
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:07,080
[sighs] I need your help.

106
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:09,457
[pensive music playing]

107
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:10,583
All right, sir.

108
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,709
What is it?

109
00:04:12,877 --> 00:04:16,839
First, I need the laptop again,

110
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:19,217
so the decoder can open it.

111
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,218
Mm.

112
00:04:20,885 --> 00:04:22,845
[in English] We're running out of time,

113
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:28,101
and the terrorist groups
are already alarmed.

114
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:32,105
Second, your new mission.

115
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:36,276
[sneaky music playing]

116
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:45,159
Mmm.

117
00:04:46,077 --> 00:04:47,578
[music continues]

118
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:50,623
Rizaldo Coloma, the mayor who's in hiding?

119
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:55,336
[in English] Yes. The corrupt mayor,
bagman of senators.

120
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:57,880
You need to find him.

121
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:02,927
Even the head of police
came to me about that.

122
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:05,972
[in English] Affirmative, sir.

123
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:10,601
You know, when you were MIA,

124
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:16,024
I sent Uno to your house
to look for the laptop.

125
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:19,152
But the kid found nothing.

126
00:05:19,235 --> 00:05:20,778
[chuckles]

127
00:05:20,862 --> 00:05:23,656
You're not just good
at finding the missing.

128
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,742
You're also good at hiding.

129
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,577
[both chuckle]

130
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:30,246
Even if they ransack that whole house,

131
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,123
even if they turn it upside down,

132
00:05:32,915 --> 00:05:34,834
they'll never find the laptop.

133
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:36,794
[both chuckle]

134
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:40,381
[theme music playing]

135
00:05:40,465 --> 00:05:42,300
[motorcycle revving]

136
00:05:42,383 --> 00:05:45,178
- [sewing machine whirring]
- [scratches]

137
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:46,763
[snipping]

138
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:50,099
[sewing machine clacking]

139
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:52,935
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

140
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:54,771
[thumps and gunshots]

141
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:55,772
[music intensifies]

142
00:05:55,855 --> 00:05:57,190
[clicking]

143
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:58,316
[snipping]

144
00:05:58,399 --> 00:06:00,151
[music swells]

145
00:06:00,234 --> 00:06:02,904
[electronic blipping]

146
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:09,118
[light music playing]

147
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:26,803
[music fades]

148
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:31,390
[suspicious music playing]

149
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:54,831
Oh? What's happening?

150
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:56,040
- [man grunts]
- Hey!

151
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:57,250
Look, Atoy is here!

152
00:06:57,333 --> 00:07:00,795
- [cheering]
- [all] Atoy! Atoy! Atoy! Atoy!

153
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:01,796
[clicks]

154
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:04,632
[suspicious music playing]

155
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:09,137
[Siony, in English] Welcome back!

156
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:10,680
Wow, this is amazing!

157
00:07:10,763 --> 00:07:12,473
- Have you eaten?
- Not yet.

158
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:15,017
- Eh, eh--did you all prepare this?
- Yes, we prepared it for you!

159
00:07:15,601 --> 00:07:18,312
[music continues]

160
00:07:22,608 --> 00:07:24,026
[gun cocking]

161
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:32,285
- [cheering]
- [lively chatter]

162
00:07:32,368 --> 00:07:34,871
- So, what do we do now?
- Let's eat.

163
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:36,747
Ah, wait, wait, wait, wait.
Let's pray first.

164
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:38,875
[Emerson] Oh, where's Father Peping?

165
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:39,667
He's not--

166
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:41,043
No, let's pray first. Where's--

167
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:41,961
I'll just call Father Peping.

168
00:07:42,044 --> 00:07:43,421
Wait. I'll look for Father.

169
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:44,672
Father Peping!

170
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:46,966
- Come on, come on, come on.
- [lively chatter]

171
00:07:47,049 --> 00:07:48,718
[ominous music playing]

172
00:07:48,801 --> 00:07:50,678
That's your biggest mistake, Atoy.

173
00:07:50,761 --> 00:07:52,555
- [tsks, sniffs]
- [music continues]

174
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:53,598
You showed yourself to me.

175
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:55,391
[ominous music fades]

176
00:07:57,143 --> 00:07:58,394
[foreboding music playing]

177
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:00,605
- [Denden] Let's pray first.
- Let's pray.

178
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:03,274
[lively chatter]

179
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:06,360
[music continues]

180
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:14,327
[Emerson hums, laughs]

181
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:15,786
Oh, well, well, well. Hmm.

182
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:18,414
[in English] If this is the heiress,

183
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:24,378
the inheritor
of all the fabrics and threads from Atoy's

184
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:26,255
and Delfin's tailoring shop, huh.

185
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:28,090
[Emerson, in English]
How have the turntables, huh?

186
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:30,801
I mean, how did the tables have turned?

187
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:32,136
Hmm?

188
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,346
[chuckles]

189
00:08:33,429 --> 00:08:34,430
What?

190
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,350
You're speaking in English!

191
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:41,312
Brother Emerson,
you're just making it hard for yourself.

192
00:08:41,395 --> 00:08:45,107
[Emerson] No, because it suits you now
to speak English, right?

193
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:47,276
What I mean is, right?

194
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,862
Who would've thought the situation
would be reversed now?

195
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:51,447
Oh, right?

196
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:54,408
You are the real daughter.

197
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:57,370
And Janine is the one without parents.

198
00:08:57,995 --> 00:09:00,414
Oh, right?

199
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:02,083
Yes, that's true.

200
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:06,420
Wait. What if…

201
00:09:06,504 --> 00:09:10,007
Atoy adopts Janine?

202
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:14,262
Are you going to do to Janine the same
mean things she did to you before?

203
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:15,388
Hmm?

204
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:17,848
- Oh, yes?
- [Emerson] Hmm?

205
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:21,727
I still remember.

206
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:23,688
- All of it!
- [Emerson] All of it?

207
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:25,690
The bullying Janine did to me.

208
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:27,567
[Emerson] Bullying. Mm-hmm.

209
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:29,610
I'll do the same to her!

210
00:09:29,694 --> 00:09:34,198
[Emerson cackling]

211
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:36,158
Just kidding!

212
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:38,035
Yes, just kidding. I know.

213
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:40,955
- Of course, I wouldn't do that.
- [Emerson] Yes.

214
00:09:41,038 --> 00:09:42,957
- It's bad to take revenge.
- [Emerson] Correct, that's bad.

215
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,710
- That's bad, mm-hmm.
- And…

216
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:48,129
I actually feel sorry for Janine.

217
00:09:48,212 --> 00:09:49,380
Yes, true.

218
00:09:49,463 --> 00:09:53,259
I hope that's what Tatoy does.

219
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:56,929
Because I also want to have a sibling, eh.

220
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:59,890
Yes, right. Correct. You're really kind.

221
00:09:59,974 --> 00:10:02,143
You know, I was just joking too.
[chuckles]

222
00:10:02,226 --> 00:10:03,436
That was just a joke, ah.

223
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:05,396
[Emerson] Don't tell Atoy that, ha.

224
00:10:05,479 --> 00:10:06,606
You, you're my favorite.

225
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:08,441
You're so cute.
You even have a ribbon in your hair.

226
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:09,692
You're so cute.

227
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:11,611
- Hmm.
- Thank you.

228
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:14,071
- [Emerson chuckles]
- Eh, Tatoy put it on me earlier.

229
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:16,073
Ah, really? It suits you.

230
00:10:16,157 --> 00:10:17,283
[pensive music playing]

231
00:10:17,366 --> 00:10:19,577
- Don't flatter me.
- [Emerson] Ah.

232
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:21,329
[giggles]

233
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:24,040
Because I won't tell on you, eh.

234
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:26,834
- There! That's why you're my favorite!
- [thumps softly]

235
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:30,129
Oh, Janine!

236
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:31,922
- Come on, let's eat!
- Janine?

237
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,050
Janine?

238
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:35,384
[suspicious music playing]

239
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:36,886
Janine! Wait, Janine!

240
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,512
[music continues]

241
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:42,224
[Peping, in English] From Thy bounty,
through Christ our Lord.

242
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:43,684
[all] Amen!

243
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,144
- [whoops, clapping]
- [in English] In the name of the Father,

244
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:46,771
the Son, the Holy Spirit.

245
00:10:46,854 --> 00:10:48,064
[all] Amen!

246
00:10:48,147 --> 00:10:49,315
- Yay!
- Oh, there! Let's eat!

247
00:10:49,398 --> 00:10:52,735
- Yay! Okay, fight!
- Let's eat! Here we go!

248
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:55,112
- [Nestor] Father, come on.
- [Father Peping] Oh! Oh.

249
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:57,073
[lively chatter]

250
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:58,366
[Nestor] Hmm. Delicious!

251
00:10:58,449 --> 00:11:00,076
[lively chatter]

252
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:01,911
- Ah, wait.
- [Nestor] Yes!

253
00:11:01,994 --> 00:11:05,081
- [Atoy] Mm!
- Ah, my glasses seem crooked, ah.

254
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:09,710
[ominous music playing]

255
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:11,796
[Father Peping] How is Audrey, Atoy?

256
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:12,922
[Atoy] She's fine.

257
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:15,883
She's just at home,
attending to something.

258
00:11:15,966 --> 00:11:17,259
But she's on her way.

259
00:11:17,343 --> 00:11:19,887
[music continues]

260
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,430
- [Atoy grunts]
- [slaps]

261
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:23,599
Don't move too much.

262
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:26,018
I'll have a hard time killing you.

263
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:27,186
[music continues]

264
00:11:27,269 --> 00:11:28,187
Father?

265
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,397
Ah, sorry.

266
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,482
There was-- there was-- an insect, eh.

267
00:11:31,565 --> 00:11:34,068
- Hi, Father!
- Ah, hello. Oh? Come on, eat.

268
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:36,570
[tense music playing]

269
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:43,369
So, you're hiding here.
That means Audrey is here too.

270
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:45,830
Brother Atoy, where's Karla?

271
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:46,914
Is she coming?

272
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:48,624
Mmm. She's just at home.

273
00:11:48,707 --> 00:11:49,792
But she's on her way too.

274
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:51,085
- Come, eat.
- All right.

275
00:11:51,168 --> 00:11:52,128
- [Siony chatters]
- I'll get some.

276
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:54,255
[music continues]

277
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:01,345
- [Siony] Oh!
- [bullet whizzes]

278
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:02,930
- [electricity crackles]
- [squeals]

279
00:12:03,013 --> 00:12:04,640
- [Siony] What was that?
- What was that?

280
00:12:05,307 --> 00:12:06,684
- [tense music]
- [Nestor] A balloon.

281
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:08,060
- Eat, eat, eat, eat!
- [T-Bak] Ah, balloon.

282
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:10,187
[Siony] Too much air.

283
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:11,564
[suspicious music playing]

284
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:14,442
Oh, there.
That insect on your face is gone.

285
00:12:15,359 --> 00:12:16,360
Insect?

286
00:12:16,444 --> 00:12:20,656
Yes, like a green firefly
that keeps moving.

287
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:22,533
[Father Peping] You didn't feel it?

288
00:12:22,616 --> 00:12:27,288
[tense music playing]

289
00:12:27,371 --> 00:12:29,123
[indistinct chatter]

290
00:12:29,206 --> 00:12:33,335
[music continues]

291
00:12:33,419 --> 00:12:36,922
[indistinct chatter]

292
00:12:37,006 --> 00:12:39,133
[suspenseful music]

293
00:12:54,773 --> 00:12:56,859
[Father Peping laughs]

294
00:12:57,443 --> 00:13:00,279
[indistinct chatter]

295
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,615
- [indistinct chatter]
- [music swells]

296
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:15,920
[suspenseful music subsides]

297
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:19,298
[Ibyang] Janine! Wait! Janine!

298
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:22,092
Where are you going?

299
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:24,887
[intense music playing]

300
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:31,727
Didn't Tatoy say
we should go to the feast?

301
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:33,854
Aren't you hungry yet?

302
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:37,608
I am hungry. But I'll endure it.

303
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:39,944
I'm shy, eh. And…

304
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:45,866
I know you don't want us
to be sisters anymore.

305
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:52,581
That's why you won't agree
for Daddy to adopt me.

306
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:54,291
Your daddy.

307
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,336
You're really stubborn.

308
00:13:57,419 --> 00:13:58,837
[mellow music playing]

309
00:13:58,921 --> 00:14:00,923
I said I'll call him Tatoy.

310
00:14:01,006 --> 00:14:02,591
I don't like "Daddy."

311
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:06,804
Sorry. I just got used to it.

312
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:08,013
[sniffs]

313
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:10,391
Oh, so you're used to that.

314
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:15,312
If you want to call him daddy,
that's your choice.

315
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:17,606
But we should…

316
00:14:19,608 --> 00:14:21,402
be sisters!

317
00:14:22,027 --> 00:14:22,945
[music continues]

318
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:25,823
Do you agree to be sisters?

319
00:14:26,448 --> 00:14:29,118
[Janine] Well, it doesn't feel real.

320
00:14:29,743 --> 00:14:32,329
I heard your conversation
with Brother Emerson.

321
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:35,624
You said you wanted to get back at me.

322
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:38,335
Huh?

323
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:40,379
[music continues]

324
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:42,673
Hah!

325
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:44,967
You didn't hear everything!

326
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:46,552
That was just a joke!

327
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:48,429
- [grunts]
- Come on.

328
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:54,435
Janine, even before…
I wanted you to be my sister.

329
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:59,565
But you always fought with me!

330
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:03,193
Let's not fight anymore, okay?

331
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:06,280
[music fades]

332
00:15:06,363 --> 00:15:10,326
[sentimental music playing]

333
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:25,633
[music fades]

334
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:28,385
[footsteps padding]

335
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:34,266
[foreboding music playing]

336
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:39,188
[footsteps approaching]

337
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:44,318
[dagger swishes]

338
00:15:44,401 --> 00:15:45,319
- [footsteps]
- [music fades]

339
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:46,695
Atoy! It's me!

340
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:47,780
Paldo!

341
00:15:48,447 --> 00:15:49,698
I almost got hit there, ah.

342
00:15:50,699 --> 00:15:51,992
Have you been here long?

343
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:53,953
No, I just arrived.

344
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:55,955
I got nervous there, ah.

345
00:15:56,830 --> 00:16:00,626
Oh? So, I didn't make it to the feast?

346
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:03,337
Didn't you see anyone else here earlier?

347
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:05,464
[suspicious music playing]

348
00:16:05,547 --> 00:16:06,382
[Paldo grunts]

349
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:08,717
None.

350
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:12,054
It's like someone tried to kill me, eh.

351
00:16:12,846 --> 00:16:14,348
[Paldo] What?

352
00:16:14,431 --> 00:16:16,141
[music continues]

353
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:18,560
Atoy, Atoy.

354
00:16:23,273 --> 00:16:25,317
[music fades]

355
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:31,407
[suspicious music playing]

356
00:16:40,582 --> 00:16:41,500
Atoy.

357
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:44,962
[music continues]

358
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:53,971
[Paldo] Atoy, this seems…

359
00:16:55,973 --> 00:16:57,433
This seems familiar to me, ah.

360
00:16:57,516 --> 00:17:00,644
[mysterious music playing]

361
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:03,981
Atoy, this belongs to Red.

362
00:17:04,064 --> 00:17:05,482
[tense music playing]

363
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:07,735
I remember he used this before.

364
00:17:10,237 --> 00:17:13,073
[music swells]

365
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:14,158
[Paldo grunts]

366
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:17,327
Oh, let's go.

367
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:19,329
Let's head to the boodle fight.

368
00:17:19,413 --> 00:17:20,789
We might run out of food.

369
00:17:20,873 --> 00:17:22,082
- They'll eat it--
- [horn honks]

370
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:26,086
- [gasps]
- [tires screeching]

371
00:17:27,212 --> 00:17:28,255
[car door lock clicks]

372
00:17:28,338 --> 00:17:29,298
[in English] Uncle Red?

373
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:30,632
[ominous music playing]

374
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:31,550
Ibyang.

375
00:17:31,633 --> 00:17:33,927
[music continues]

376
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:34,845
[groans]

377
00:17:36,013 --> 00:17:37,139
[suspenseful music]

378
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:39,516
- [Ibyang groans]
- [grunting]

379
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,018
You're the wicked bald man!

380
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:42,728
Hey! Let go of the child!

381
00:17:42,811 --> 00:17:44,229
Get your filthy hands off of Ibyang!

382
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:45,856
- No! Let me go!
- [grunts, thumps]

383
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:47,024
Brother Kurt! [gasps]

384
00:17:47,107 --> 00:17:48,067
Brother Kurt!

385
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:49,860
- [Ibyang] Come on!
- [Janine] Help me!

386
00:17:49,943 --> 00:17:51,612
- [grunts]
- Get in!

387
00:17:51,695 --> 00:17:52,988
Help! Brother Kurt!

388
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:54,364
- Get in!
- [Red] Faster!

389
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:57,284
- [tense dramatic music]
- [tires screeching]

390
00:17:57,367 --> 00:18:00,162
[dramatic music]

391
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:01,330
Sir.

392
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:03,540
Sir, sorry. But Boss called.

393
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:05,084
He wants a follow-up on the laptop.

394
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:07,419
He said it's needed now
so the decoder can open it.

395
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:08,337
All right.

396
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,296
Let's go.

397
00:18:09,379 --> 00:18:13,383
[phone ringing]

398
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:14,635
- Brother Kurt?
- [Kurt] <i>Atoy?</i>

399
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:18,347
[in English] Ibyang and Janine,
they've uh-- they've been taken.

400
00:18:18,931 --> 00:18:20,599
[in English] Taken?
Wha-- what do you mean taken?

401
00:18:20,682 --> 00:18:24,436
They were loaded into a black SUV by a…

402
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:25,729
[in English] like a bald guy!

403
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:29,274
That's Red. Where are you?

404
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:30,859
Do you know where they went?

405
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:32,820
[music fades]

406
00:18:32,903 --> 00:18:35,030
It's good that you and Atoy are okay now.

407
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:36,490
I'm really happy too.

408
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:38,492
Thank God.

409
00:18:38,575 --> 00:18:39,535
[chuckles softly]

410
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:40,953
Ah, wait. Mmm.

411
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:42,538
[Cita] Fabric.

412
00:18:42,621 --> 00:18:44,373
- Ah, hello.
- Hi!

413
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:46,375
Is Atoy here?

414
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:48,502
He just stepped out.

415
00:18:49,336 --> 00:18:52,631
Aren't you the one
who was kidnapped with Atoy?

416
00:18:52,714 --> 00:18:57,344
Yes. That's why I came here, to thank him.

417
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:00,639
Ah. Well, better come with us.

418
00:19:00,722 --> 00:19:02,975
We're heading to him now, eh.

419
00:19:03,058 --> 00:19:04,059
Audrey, you too.

420
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:06,478
Don't worry, Atoy is there.

421
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:07,604
Nothing will happen to you.

422
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:09,523
The kids are already there.

423
00:19:09,606 --> 00:19:11,692
[ominous music playing]

424
00:19:11,775 --> 00:19:13,443
Miss Cita, we have a problem.

425
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:18,282
Sorry. But you can't go out yet,
it's dangerous.

426
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:19,533
Wait. Why?

427
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,411
Paldo, what happened? Where's Atoy?

428
00:19:22,494 --> 00:19:24,163
Where are the kids? Ibyang?

429
00:19:24,246 --> 00:19:25,914
- Janine?
- They were abducted by Red.

430
00:19:25,998 --> 00:19:27,583
- [Cita] What?!
- What?!

431
00:19:27,666 --> 00:19:28,750
[gasps]

432
00:19:28,834 --> 00:19:30,502
And Sir Atoy is chasing them now.

433
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:32,921
Paldo.

434
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:34,590
[tense music playing]

435
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:36,425
[gasps] How--

436
00:19:36,508 --> 00:19:39,720
[music continues]

437
00:19:39,803 --> 00:19:41,263
What do we do?

438
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:43,599
My god, the children.

439
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:46,226
[gasps]

440
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:47,436
[tense music fades]

441
00:19:47,519 --> 00:19:49,438
We're planning to pass
through the highway.

442
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:51,023
[man] Then give the food to the poor.

443
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:52,232
- [T-Bak] Oh, mmm.
- [Siony] Ah, is that so?

444
00:19:52,316 --> 00:19:53,483
- [Denden] Oh, there you go.
- [T-Bak] You thought---

445
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:54,902
You judged too quickly.

446
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:56,361
- Here, let me help you.
- [woman] Ah, here.

447
00:19:56,445 --> 00:19:58,822
- [woman] Give them, give them.
- There's still plenty of tilapia left.

448
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:00,741
Here, Father, we'll just wrap it.

449
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:02,826
- They'll give it away.
- [Siony] What a waste.

450
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,786
I'll take this, Father.

451
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:05,704
Hmm.

452
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:08,373
[T-Bak] Let's pair it with tomatoes too.

453
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:10,042
[indistinct chatter]

454
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:12,711
- Let's fill this up, oh.
- Karla.

455
00:20:13,337 --> 00:20:16,173
Can I talk to you in private?

456
00:20:16,256 --> 00:20:17,633
[light music playing]

457
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:19,760
[Denden] <i>If a guy really likes you,</i>
<i>you won't be confused</i>

458
00:20:19,843 --> 00:20:20,969
whether he really likes you.

459
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:22,888
He'll tell you directly.

460
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,974
- [in English] Correct.
- Mmm.

461
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:28,685
But Gavin still seems taken.

462
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:31,521
I saw him with Cathy,
they were together earlier.

463
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:32,689
[music swells]

464
00:20:32,773 --> 00:20:33,732
Ah, no.

465
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:35,651
My boyfriend might get mad.

466
00:20:35,734 --> 00:20:37,861
Boyfriend? You already have a boyfriend?

467
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:38,820
Who?

468
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:40,989
Uno!

469
00:20:42,699 --> 00:20:44,284
You said yes to him? That was fast.

470
00:20:44,993 --> 00:20:46,286
Is that bad?

471
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:49,414
Well, you and Cathy,
after one date, you were already together.

472
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:51,041
But if it's us, it's bad?

473
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:54,336
[pensive music playing]

474
00:20:55,879 --> 00:20:57,506
[Emerson] Where are they? Where are…

475
00:20:57,589 --> 00:20:59,091
[music continues]

476
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:00,008
Karla.

477
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:02,678
Did you see…

478
00:21:02,761 --> 00:21:04,638
Janine and Ibyang?

479
00:21:04,721 --> 00:21:05,764
I've been looking for them.

480
00:21:05,847 --> 00:21:07,266
Aren't they here?

481
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:08,684
No, brother.

482
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:11,019
Oh, no, I'm in trouble.

483
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:13,063
I'm in trouble with Atoy.

484
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:14,356
[tense music playing]

485
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:17,401
I was assigned
to be the nanny for the kids.

486
00:21:19,444 --> 00:21:21,113
Where could they be?

487
00:21:28,912 --> 00:21:31,164
Are you sure
there's no one at the Regalias?

488
00:21:31,248 --> 00:21:32,666
[line rings]

489
00:21:32,749 --> 00:21:33,625
[Atoy] No one.

490
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:36,670
I searched the whole house.
The kids weren't there.

491
00:21:36,753 --> 00:21:38,672
Only the maids were around.

492
00:21:40,257 --> 00:21:43,552
Gavin, do you know where your parents
might have taken the kids?

493
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:45,679
I don't know, Brother Atoy.

494
00:21:45,762 --> 00:21:48,557
Oh, no. Where could they
have taken the children?

495
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:49,891
I hope they're not hurt.

496
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:51,852
I hope nothing happened to them.

497
00:21:51,935 --> 00:21:53,437
I spoke with Sir Mercado.

498
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:55,355
He said they'll send a team to go around.

499
00:21:56,189 --> 00:21:57,983
We really need to talk to Red.

500
00:21:58,066 --> 00:22:00,652
I keep calling him, but he won't answer!

501
00:22:01,278 --> 00:22:03,864
Try again, try again.

502
00:22:03,947 --> 00:22:06,783
[line ringing]

503
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:08,118
[line blips]

504
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:09,786
Red!

505
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:11,955
Oh, what do you want?

506
00:22:12,039 --> 00:22:14,249
[Audrey, in English]
Red, where the hell are my daughters?!

507
00:22:14,750 --> 00:22:16,084
You animal!

508
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:17,002
[Red on the phone, in English] <i>Daughters?</i>

509
00:22:17,085 --> 00:22:19,713
Nice, huh. So, what are you now?
A happy family?

510
00:22:19,796 --> 00:22:21,089
Hello, Red!

511
00:22:21,173 --> 00:22:23,216
You animal! You're a demon!

512
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:25,385
Where are the kids?
Give me back the children!

513
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:28,263
Stupid. What are you, Atoy?

514
00:22:28,847 --> 00:22:31,266
I worked hard to take the kids,
and then I'll just give them back?

515
00:22:31,349 --> 00:22:32,225
What am I, dumb?

516
00:22:32,309 --> 00:22:33,685
What do you want, huh?!

517
00:22:33,769 --> 00:22:35,937
Money?! What? Me?!

518
00:22:36,021 --> 00:22:38,607
Am I what you want?
I'm the one you're targeting, right?

519
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:40,358
Come after me. Come on!

520
00:22:40,442 --> 00:22:42,444
[Atoy] <i>Don't involve the children!</i>
<i>You animal!</i>

521
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:43,987
[suspicious music playing]

522
00:22:44,071 --> 00:22:45,489
That was earlier, eh.

523
00:22:45,572 --> 00:22:46,948
But now I feel like
doing something else, eh.

524
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:49,659
What do you really want, huh?!

525
00:22:49,743 --> 00:22:51,453
[Red, in English] <i>Nothing.</i>
<i>Just to hurt you.</i>

526
00:22:51,536 --> 00:22:53,080
You, Audrey.

527
00:22:53,163 --> 00:22:54,623
You're the favorite child, right?

528
00:22:54,706 --> 00:22:55,749
And now, you're happy?

529
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:58,794
[Red] <i>That's nonsense. Dad's gone.</i>

530
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:01,213
So now I can do whatever I want.

531
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:05,717
I'll make these kids suffer.

532
00:23:05,801 --> 00:23:06,843
I'll profit from them.

533
00:23:06,927 --> 00:23:08,095
[heavy music playing]

534
00:23:08,178 --> 00:23:09,137
[in English] But don't worry.

535
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:11,264
[Red] <i>I'll send you pictures.</i>

536
00:23:11,348 --> 00:23:13,225
<i>So you'll know where they're going.</i>

537
00:23:13,308 --> 00:23:15,018
And what condition they're in.

538
00:23:16,144 --> 00:23:18,146
And I'll make an album of it,

539
00:23:18,230 --> 00:23:20,774
showing how their situation worsens.

540
00:23:20,857 --> 00:23:21,983
[in English] Just for you guys.

541
00:23:22,067 --> 00:23:23,860
- No, no, no, no! Hello!
- No!

542
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:25,737
[tense music playing]

543
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:28,448
[tense dramatic music]

544
00:23:34,371 --> 00:23:36,581
- Red, where are you?! Hello!
- No!

545
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:40,168
- [gasps]
- [music continues]

546
00:23:43,338 --> 00:23:44,631
- Aargh!
- [grunts]

547
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:49,010
- What do we do?
- Call him.

548
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:56,059
- [electronic blipping]
- [intense music playing]

549
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:00,397
Don't worry.

550
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,356
‪UP NEXT

551
00:24:01,439 --> 00:24:03,692
Tatoy will save us.

552
00:24:03,775 --> 00:24:04,860
He's good at finding people and things!

553
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:06,611
[theme music playing]

554
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:08,029
What if he doesn't?

555
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:09,281
What will they do to us?

556
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,074
Will they torture us?

557
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:12,617
Kill us?

558
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:16,580
It seems like human trafficking
has long been the trade on that island.

559
00:24:17,164 --> 00:24:21,334
We really need to expose that place,
so their illegal business stops.

560
00:24:21,418 --> 00:24:24,963
But isn't it true,
to get inside and save Ibyang

561
00:24:25,046 --> 00:24:27,340
and Janine, you need to win
the drag show contest, right?

562
00:24:29,134 --> 00:24:33,346
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

563
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:37,559
[drag queen] Hello, ladies!

564
00:24:37,642 --> 00:24:39,227
What's your group's name?

565
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:41,396
Us? Oh, we are the…

566
00:24:42,105 --> 00:24:45,734
[all] Karayom Kweens!

567
00:24:45,817 --> 00:24:46,693
That's them.

568
00:24:46,776 --> 00:24:48,195
That's the Glitter Bombz.

569
00:24:48,278 --> 00:24:49,613
[Emerson] Their dances are really fierce.

570
00:24:49,696 --> 00:24:52,824
They own the killer… death drop!

571
00:24:52,908 --> 00:24:55,243
No matter what happens,
we need to beat them.

572
00:24:55,327 --> 00:24:57,329
- [audience cheering]
- [theme music continues]

573
00:24:57,412 --> 00:24:58,580
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

574
00:24:58,663 --> 00:25:01,124
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

575
00:25:01,208 --> 00:25:04,461
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

576
00:25:04,544 --> 00:25:05,921
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

577
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:08,173
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
